  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to create a function `word_histogram` that processes an input string and computes the frequency of each word, ignoring case and punctuation. Here's how you can do it:\n\n### Step-by-step Explanation\n\n1. **Normalize the string:**\n   - Convert all characters to lowercase using the `lower()` method.\n2. **Remove punctuation:**\n   - Printing out all punctuation marks helps identify which characters to exclude.\n   - Example of punctuation:  !\"#$%&'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\]^_`{|}~\n3. **Split the string into words:**\n   - Use the `split()` method on the processed string to separate words.\n4. **Create a dictionary (`Counter` for simplicity):**\n   - Use an empty dictionary to store word frequencies.\n\n### Implementation\n\n```python\ndef word_histogram(s):\n    s = s.lower()\n    punctuation = '!\"#$%&\\'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\]^_`{|}~'\n    for char in punctuation:\n        s = s.replace(char, ' ')\n    words = s.split()\n    return dict(Counter(words))\n```",
